# notebooks/wallet_toxicity_frame.csv is tracked on purpose. It has a producer,
# data/build_toxicity_frame.py, but rebuilding it needs the book panel, which needs the
# raw archive and credentials a reader may not have. It holds counterparty-level
# aggregates keyed by an integer index, not by address.
# wallet_toxicity_frame.csv  -- deliberately NOT ignored

# Scratch notebook execution copies (determinism / clean-run checks)
notebooks/_nb_*.ipynb

# Local exploration and scratch harnesses
probes/probe_battery*
probes/round2_battery*
probes/round3_battery*

# Credentials. None are committed today, and these lines are here so that an accident
# cannot make one: rebuilding the intermediates from the live archives reads two
# requester-pays buckets, so that route needs AWS keys, and they belong in the
# environment or in a profile outside this tree rather than in any file inside it.
# CONFIG.md, section "AWS access", states the rule in prose and names `.env*`; this is
# what enforces it. None of the names carries a slash, on purpose: a pattern without
# one matches at every depth, so an environment file dropped in a subdirectory is
# excluded as surely as one at the root.
.env*
*.env
credentials
.aws/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_ed25519
